{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on END 3743d64a, CE-2: do not change the expectation of the\nNative case. Change the answer of `settle`.\n\nThe case \"a page that answered first leaves custody to the scope's\nanswer\" holds an acceptance fact of NF-5: `settle` of a request\nwith no decisive answer says `answer: \"unknown\"` and\n`phase: \"unknown\"`, and sends nothing. CE-2 must keep that fact.\nAt head `d1beb6f0`, `absenceRecovery` returns a custody failure for\neach state, so a record that stays unknown now answers as an\nerror. Act 89723f22 stated that shape and I did not object then.\nThe Native case shows what it changes.\n\n1. A proof that ends nothing answers with the unknown report of\n   NF-2, as before CE-2: the `ok` shape with `answer: \"unknown\"`,\n   the phase of the record, the steps, `outcomes` and `attempt`.\n   This covers `unproved` with each reason, `present`, and a\n   record that changed during the recovery.\n2. The reason of the proof goes into `sentence`. Your sentences\n   for the states stand, shortened if the report needs it.\n3. `next` names both ways for a request past its expiry: call the\n   original tool again with the same key, which sends the same\n   envelope and gets the answer of the scope, or call `settle`\n   again after the scope records a later entry.\n4. Only a proved absence uses the custody failure, with your\n   wording for `unsent`. That is the ruled shape.\n5. The repeated CLI install follows the same rule. A proof that\n   ends nothing keeps the exit code and the first line that an\n   unknown install has, and adds the reason. If the CLI has no\n   such line today, tell me what it prints.\n\nReasons. An agent decides on `answer`. The record did not change,\nso the answer must not change. The report carries the phase and\nthe steps, and the failure drops them. An error marks a call that\ncould not do its work, and this call did its work. Item 4 of\nruling d264dea5 says that the answer shapes of NF-2 stay.\n\nTests. The old assertion of the Native case stays as it is. Add\nthe assertion on the reason beside it. The witness of 256 requests\nand the case at 1 ms before the expiry expect the unknown report\nwith the reason.\n\nThis is a production change, so the head takes one new full gate,\nas you said. Run the inventory owner and the pins before the START\nif a tool description changes.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}